but still it is his portion, his dear ones to see, and to reach
his high-roofed house, and his own fatherland.”

And so, when with Iasion fine-plaited Demeter,
yielding to her own heart, was mingled in love and in bed
in a thrice-ploughed fallow field;

But since there is no way that the mind of aegis-bearing Zeus
any other god should either slip past or bring to nothing,
let him go to ruin, if that one urges him on and commands it,
over the unharvested sea;

And I, bread and water and red wine
will put aboard, all you could desire, to keep hunger from you,
and clothes I will put about you;

“Something else, surely, you, goddess, are devising in this, and not at all my convoy,
you who bid me on a raft to cross the great gulf of the sea,
dread and grievous;
